    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0407" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2205</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 216</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-06">April 6, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        14.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Leticia peace negotiations.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with recent telegrams from
                    this Embassy on the subject cited above, I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    copies, in translation, of the statements recently issued by the Chairman of the
                    Colombian and Peruvian delegations to the Leticia peace conference.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh Gibson</hi></signed></closer>



